    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's denote the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters Jamie has as \\( n \\). Since the number of each type of coin is the same, Jamie has \\( n \\) nickels, \\( n \\) dimes, and \\( n \\) quarters.\n\nFirst, we need to determine the value of each type of coin in cents. A nickel is worth 5 cents, a dime is worth 10 cents, and a quarter is worth 25 cents. Therefore, the total value of the coins in the jar can be expressed as:\n\\[\n5n + 10n + 25n\n\\]\n\nCombining the terms, we get:\n\\[\n5n + 10n + 25n = 40n\n\\]\n\nWe know that the total value of the coins is \\$13.20, which is equivalent to 1320 cents. So, we set up the equation:\n\\[\n40n = 1320\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( n \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 40:\n\\[\nn = \\frac{1320}{40} = 33\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Jamie has \\(\\boxed{33}\\) nickels.",
