    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of nickels Jamie has. Let's denote the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters as \\( n \\).\n\nFirst, we know the value of each type of coin:\n- A nickel is worth \\$0.05.\n- A dime is worth \\$0.10.\n- A quarter is worth \\$0.25.\n\nThe total value of the coins in the jar is given as \\$13.20. Since the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters is the same, we can express the total value as:\n\\[ 0.05n + 0.10n + 0.25n = 13.20 \\]\n\nNext, we combine the terms on the left side of the equation:\n\\[ (0.05 + 0.10 + 0.25)n = 13.20 \\]\n\\[ 0.40n = 13.20 \\]\n\nTo find \\( n \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 0.40:\n\\[ n = \\frac{13.20}{0.40} \\]\n\\[ n = 33 \\]\n\nTherefore, Jamie has \\(\\boxed{33}\\) nickels.",
