    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the number of nickels Jamie has, we start by defining the number of each type of coin and then use the given total value of the coins to set up an equation.\n\nLet \\( x \\) be the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters Jamie has. Since each coin has a certain value, we can express the total value in terms of \\( x \\).\n\nThe value of one nickel is $0.05, the value of one dime is $0.10, and the value of one quarter is $0.25. Therefore, the total value of the nickels is \\( 0.05x \\), the total value of the dimes is \\( 0.10x \\), and the total value of the quarters is \\( 0.25x \\).\n\nThe sum of these values is given as $13.20. Thus, we can write the equation:\n\\[\n0.05x + 0.10x + 0.25x = 13.20\n\\]\n\nCombining the terms on the left side, we get:\n\\[\n0.40x = 13.20\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 0.40:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{13.20}{0.40} = 33\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Jamie has \\(\\boxed{33}\\) nickels.",
